ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "fix for infinite loop in split_graphemes\n\nFix for https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues/3958"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in rich/cells.py (hunk at line 186).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"rich/cells.py\", \"old_text\": \"    SPECIAL = {\\\"\\\\u200d\\\", \\\"\\\\ufe0f\\\"}\\n    while index < codepoint_count:\\n        if (character := text[index]) in SPECIAL:\\n            if character == \\\"\\\\u200d\\\":\\n                # zero width joiner\\n                index += 2\\n                if spans:\\n                    start, _end, cell_length = spans[-1]\\n                    spans[-1] = (start, index, cell_length)\\n            elif last_measured_character:\\n                # variation selector 16\\n                index += 1\\n                if spans:\\n                    start, _end, cell_length = spans[-1]\\n                    if last_measured_character in cell_table.narrow_to_wide:\\n                        last_measured_character = None\\n                        cell_length += 1\\n                        total_width += 1\\n                    spans[-1] = (start, index, cell_length)\\n            continue\\n\\n        if character_width := get_character_cell_size(character, unicode_version):\\n            last_measured_character = character\\n            spans.append((index, index := index + 1, character_width))\\n            total_width += character_width\\n        elif spans:\\n            # zero width characters are associated with the previous character\\n            start, _end, cell_length = spans[-1]\\n            spans[-1] = (start, index := index + 1, cell_length)\\n\\n    return (spans, total_width)\\n\", \"new_text\": \"    SPECIAL = {\\\"\\\\u200d\\\", \\\"\\\\ufe0f\\\"}\\n    while index < codepoint_count:\\n        if (character := text[index]) in SPECIAL:\\n            if not spans:\\n                # ZWJ or variation selector at the beginning of the string doesn't really make sense.\\n                # But handle it, we must.\\n                spans.append((index, index := index + 1, 0))\\n                continue\\n            if character == \\\"\\\\u200d\\\":\\n                # zero width joiner\\n                # The condition handles the case where a ZWJ is at the end of the string, and has nothing to join\\n                index += 2 if index < (codepoint_count - 1) else 1\\n                start, _end, cell_length = spans[-1]\\n                spans[-1] = (start, index, cell_length)\\n            else:\\n                # variation selector 16\\n                index += 1\\n                if last_measured_character:\\n                    start, _end, cell_length = spans[-1]\\n                    if last_measured_character in cell_table.narrow_to_wide:\\n                        last_measured_character = None\\n                        cell_length += 1\\n                        total_width += 1\\n                    spans[-1] = (start, index, cell_length)\\n                else:\\n                    # No previous character to change the size of.\\n                    # Shouldn't occur in practice.\\n                    # But handle it, we must.\\n                    start, _end, cell_length = spans[-1]\\n                    spans[-1] = (start, index, cell_length)\\n            continue\\n\\n        if character_width := get_character_cell_size(character, unicode_version):\\n            last_measured_character = character\\n            spans.append((index, index := index + 1, character_width))\\n            total_width += character_width\\n        else:\\n            # Character has zero width\\n            if spans:\\n                # zero width characters are associated with the previous character\\n                start, _end, cell_length = spans[-1]\\n                spans[-1] = (start, index := index + 1, cell_length)\\n            else:\\n                # A zero width character with no prior spans\\n                spans.append((index, index := index + 1, 0))\\n\\n    return (spans, total_width)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "rich_4006", "repo": "Textualize/rich", "base_commit": "27701029082052c6541031b6f139097230253900", "files": ["rich/cells.py"], "symbols": ["_cell_len", "split_graphemes", "append", "of"], "n_hunks": 2, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_cells.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live tool outputs. Read-file observations are snapshot.", "turns": 12, "generator": "gen_programmatic.py v1", "traj_turn": 7, "tool": "edit_file", "est_tokens": 1926, "split_from": "rich_4006"}}
