dling of JSON Schema attributes named \"$ref\"\r\n\r\nRelated to: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/14344"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Before editing anything, I'll write a small repro script under /tmp that triggers the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/repro_fastapi_14349.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Repro for fastapi_14349 (programmatic replay; generic script).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/workspace\\\")\\n\\nfrom fastapi._compat.v2 import _replace_refs  # noqa: F401\\n\\n# Reported failure (from the issue):\\n# \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix handling of JSON Schema attributes named \\\"$ref\\\" Fix handling of JSON Schema attributes named \\\"$ref\\\" Related to: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/14344\\n# A faithful repro needs the exact failing call from the issue, so\\n# this script confirms the module imports and the symbol exists;\\n# the failure itself is triggered from the issue's example.\\nprint(\\\"repro ready:\\\", _replace_refs)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "File written."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Running the repro to confirm the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_14349.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "FAIL: \ud83d\udc1b Fix handling of JSON Schema attributes named \"$ref\" Fix handling of JSON Schema attributes named \"$ref\" Related to: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/14344"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/_compat/v2.py (hunk at line 262).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/_compat/v2.py\", \"old_text\": \"    new_schema = deepcopy(schema)\\n    for key, value in new_schema.items():\\n        if key == \\\"$ref\\\":\\n            ref_name = schema[\\\"$ref\\\"].split(\\\"/\\\")[-1]\\n            if ref_name in old_name_to_new_name_map:\\n                new_name = old_name_to_new_name_map[ref_name]\\n                new_schema[\\\"$ref\\\"] = REF_TEMPLATE.format(model=new_name)\\n            else:\\n                new_schema[\\\"$ref\\\"] = schema[\\\"$ref\\\"]\\n            continue\\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\\n            new_schema[key] = _replace_refs(\", \"new_text\": \"    new_schema = deepcopy(schema)\\n    for key, value in new_schema.items():\\n        if key == \\\"$ref\\\":\\n            value = schema[\\\"$ref\\\"]\\n            if isinstance(value, str):\\n                ref_name = schema[\\\"$ref\\\"].split(\\\"/\\\")[-1]\\n                if ref_name in old_name_to_new_name_map:\\n                    new_name = old_name_to_new_name_map[ref_name]\\n                    new_schema[\\\"$ref\\\"] = REF_TEMPLATE.format(model=new_name)\\n            continue\\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\\n            new_schema[key] = _replace_refs(\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Re-running the repro after the edit to check the fix.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_14349.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "PASS: repro script now succeeds (no failure output after the fix)."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Repro passes. Now the narrowest relevant tests.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python -m pytest tests/test_schema_ref_pydantic_v2.py -q\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_14349", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "eaf611f9ee56de4f16c837d4f487a4b9fca507c4", "files": ["fastapi/_compat/v2.py"], "symbols": ["_replace_refs", "split", "format"], "n_hunks": 1, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_schema_ref_pydantic_v2.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_o