1009\t    and add `patch_index` to the corresponding meta data.\n  1010\t    And will return a list of dictionaries for all the cropped images.\n  1011\t    If a dimension of the expected spatial size is bigger than the input image size,\n  1012\t    will not crop that dimension. So the cropped result may be smaller than the expected size,\n  1013\t    and the cropped results of several images may not have exactly the same shape.\n  1014\t\n  1015\t    Args:\n  1016\t        image_keys: Keys to pick image data for transformation. They need to have the same spatial size.\n  1017\t        box_keys: The single key to pick box data for transformation. The box mode is assumed to be ``StandardMode``.\n  1018\t        label_keys: Keys that represent the labels corresponding to the ``box_keys``. Multiple keys are allowed.\n  1019\t        spatial_size: the spatial size of the crop region e.g. [224, 224, 128].\n  1020\t            if a dimension of ROI size is bigger than image size, will not crop that dimension of the image.\n  1021\t            if its components have non-positive values, the corresponding size of `data[label_key]` will be used.\n  1022\t            for example: if the spatial size of input data is [40, 40, 40] and `spatial_size=[32, 64, -1]`,\n  1023\t            the spatial size of output data will be [32, 40, 40].\n  1024\t        pos: used with `neg` together to calculate the ratio ``pos / (pos + neg)`` for the probability\n  1025\t            to pick a foreground voxel as a center rather than a background voxel."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"read_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/Project-MONAI__MONAI__0.9/monai/apps/detection/transforms/dictionary.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESULT of [str_replace_editor]:\nHere's the result of running `cat -n` on /workspace/Project-MONAI__MONAI__0.9/monai/apps/detection/transforms/dictionary.py:\n  1025\t            to pick a foreground voxel as a center rather than a background voxel.\n  1026\t        neg: used with `pos` together to calculate the ratio ``pos / (pos + neg)`` for the probability\n  1027\t            to pick a foreground voxel as a center rather than a background voxel.\n  1028\t        num_samples: number of samples (crop regions) to take in each list.\n  1029\t        whole_box: Bool, default True, whether we prefer to contain at least one whole box in the cropped foreground patch.\n  1030\t            Even if True, it is still possible to get partial box if there are multiple boxes in the image.\n  1031\t        thresh_image_key: if thresh_image_key is not None, use ``label == 0 & thresh_image > image_threshold`` to select\n  1032\t            the negative sample(background) center. so the crop center will only exist on valid image area.\n  1033\t        image_threshold: if enabled thresh_image_key, use ``thresh_image > image_threshold`` to determine\n  1034\t            the valid image content area.\n  1035\t        fg_indices_key: if provided pre-computed foreground indices of `label`, will ignore above `image_key` and\n  1036\t            `image_threshold`, and randomly select crop centers based on them, need to provide `fg_indices_key`\n  1037\t            and `bg_indices_key` together, expect to be 1 dim array of spatial indices after flattening.\n  1038\t            a typical usage is to call `FgBgToIndicesd` transform first and cache the results.\n  1039\t        bg_indices_key: if provided pre-computed background indices of `label`, will ignore above `image_key` and\n  1040\t            `image_threshold`, and randomly select crop centers based on them, need to provide `fg_indices_key`\n  1041\t            and `bg_indices_key` together, expect to be 1 dim array of spatial indices after flattening.\n  1\n[... observation truncated ...]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"read_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/Project-MONAI__MONAI__0