outer.routes` (e.g. Jupyverse)\n\n## Pull Request\r\n\r\n\u2728 Add `iter_route_contexts()` for advanced use cases that used to use `router.routes` (e.g. Jupyverse)\r\n\r\nRelated to: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/15782\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease start with a GitHub Discussion.\r\n\r\nOnce a team member asks you to open a PR, create it and link the discussion here.\r\n\r\nObvious typo fixes can be made in a PR without starting a discussion.\r\n-->\r\n\r\nDiscussion: <!-- Link to the GitHub Discussion -->\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\n<!-- Write the description of your PR here -->\r\n\r\n## AI Disclaimer\r\n\r\nCodex with GPT 5.5 through several iterations, defining and trimming the interface.\r\n\r\nManual review of all the code.\r\n\r\n<!-- If using AI, write here the prompt and model used -->\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>AI transcript</summary>\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste here the entire AI transcript -->\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] This PR is an obvious typo fix, or it links to a GitHub Discussion for the proposed code change.\r\n- [ ] I added tests for the change.\r\n- [ ] The new or updated tests fail on the main branch and pass on this PR.\r\n- [ ] Coverage stays at 100%.\r\n- [ ] The documentation explains the change if needed.\r\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/openapi/utils.py (hunk at line 527).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/openapi/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"    openapi_version: str = \\\"3.1.0\\\",\\n    summary: str | None = None,\\n    description: str | None = None,\\n    routes: Sequence[BaseRoute],\\n    webhooks: Sequence[BaseRoute] | None = None,\\n    tags: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\\n    servers: list[dict[str, str | Any]] | None = None,\\n    terms_of_service: str | None = None,\", \"new_text\": \"    openapi_version: str = \\\"3.1.0\\\",\\n    summary: str | None = None,\\n    description: str | None = None,\\n    routes: Sequence[BaseRoute | routing.RouteContext],\\n    webhooks: Sequence[BaseRoute | routing.RouteContext] | None = None,\\n    tags: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\\n    servers: list[dict[str, str | Any]] | None = None,\\n    terms_of_service: str | None = None,\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/openapi/utils.py (hunk at line 563).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/openapi/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"        model_name_map=model_name_map,\\n        separate_input_output_schemas=separate_input_output_schemas,\\n    )\\n    for route, route_context in routing._iter_routes_with_context(routes):\\n        api_route = _get_api_route_for_openapi(route, route_context)\\n        if api_route is not None:\\n            result = get_openapi_path(\\n                route=api_route,\", \"new_text\": \"        model_name_map=model_name_map,\\n        separate_input_output_schemas=separate_input_output_schemas,\\n    )\\n    for route_context in routing.iter_route_contexts(routes):\\n        api_route = _get_api_route_for_openapi(route_context)\\n        if api_route is not None:\\n            result = get_openapi_path(\\n                route=api_route,\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_15785", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "202b2d2f5f331db9102b5dbcef071a9e09bed10e", "files": ["fastapi/openapi/utils.py", "fastapi/routing.py"], "symbols": ["get_openapi_path", "_get_api_route_for_openapi", "get_fields_from_routes", "get_openapi"], "n_hunks": 6, "n_files": 2, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_router_include_context.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Progra