sly discussed in https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/11424 with the PR at https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/11425\r\n\r\nSince I made modifications in the fork of the repo, the PR was automatically closed. This PR serves to add the circular reference check again. Discussed again in https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/14251"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll localize with the graph tools first, starting from the symbols named in the issue.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"search_similar_code\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"read_users\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"symbol\": \"read_users\",\n \"matches\": [\n  {\n   \"file\": \"fastapi/routing.py\",\n   \"line\": 732,\n   \"kind\": \"definition\"\n  }\n ]\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "read_users is defined in fastapi/routing.py. Checking its callers and callees before reading any file.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_neighbors\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"read_users\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"symbol\": \"read_users\",\n \"callers\": [],\n \"callees\": [],\n \"note\": \"neighbors derived from symbols co-occurring in the patch\"\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Getting the surrounding call graph so I read only the files that matter.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_subgraph\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"read_users\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_14258", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "e94028ab60d18080810910352bc9129e8046c92d", "files": ["fastapi/routing.py"], "symbols": ["read_users"], "n_hunks": 1, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_router_circular_import.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Pro