e '[1]' is invalid for input of size 2\" confirms the issue when the batch size is greater than 1. The problem likely lies in how the SSIM values are being concatenated and reshaped.\n\nTo resolve this, I'll modify the `SSIMLoss` class to handle batch sizes greater than 1 more effectively. Instead of iterating over each item in the batch and concatenating the results, we can directly compute the SSIM for the entire batch using vectorized operations. This approach will be more efficient and should resolve the error.\n\nLet's proceed with modifying the source code to implement this fix.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/Project-MONAI__MONAI__1.1/monai/losses/ssim_loss.py\", \"old_text\": \"\\n        if x.shape[0] == 1:\\n            ssim_value: torch.Tensor = SSIMMetric(\\n                data_range, self.win_size, self.k1, self.k2, self.spatial_dims\\n            )._compute_tensor(x, y)\\n        elif x.shape[0] > 1:\\n\\n            for i in range(x.shape[0]):\\n                ssim_val: torch.Tensor = SSIMMetric(\\n                    data_range, self.win_size, self.k1, self.k2, self.spatial_dims\\n                )._compute_tensor(x[i : i + 1], y[i : i + 1])\\n                if i == 0:\\n                    ssim_value = ssim_val\\n                else:\\n                    ssim_value = torch.cat((ssim_value.view(1), ssim_val.view(1)), dim=0)\\n\\n        else:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Batch size is not nonnegative integer value\\\")\\n        # 1- dimensional tensor is only allowed\\n        ssim_value = ssim_value.view(-1, 1)\\n\", \"new_text\": \"\\n        ssim_metric = SSIMMetric(data_range, self.win_size, self.k1, self.k2, self.spatial_dims)\\n        ssim_value = ssim_metric._compute_tensor(x, y)\\n        if ssim_value.dim() > 1:\\n            ssim_value = ssim_value.mean(dim=[1, 2, 3] if self.spatial_dims == 2 else [1, 2, 3, 4])\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESUL