all|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/reproduce_error.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESULT of [execute_bash]:\npython /workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/reproduce_error.py\r\nResponse: {'ResponseMetadata': {'HTTPStatusCode': 200, 'HTTPHeaders': {'server': 'amazon.com', 'date': 'Mon, 04 Nov 2024 00:33:20 GMT'}, 'RetryAttempts': 0}}\r\nResponse: {'ResponseMetadata': {'HTTPStatusCode': 200, 'HTTPHeaders': {'server': 'amazon.com', 'date': 'Mon, 04 Nov 2024 00:33:20 GMT'}, 'RetryAttempts': 0}}\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/reproduce_error.py\", line 78, in <module>\r\n    test_send_email()\r\n  File \"/testbed/moto/core/models.py\", line 128, in wrapper\r\n    result = func(*args, **kwargs)\r\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"/workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/reproduce_error.py\", line 43, in test_send_email\r\n    assert \"mocked-message-id\" in response, \"The send_email method did not return the expected mocked response.\"\r\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\nAssertionError: The send_email method did not return the expected mocked response.[Python Interpreter: /opt/miniconda3/envs/testbed/bin/python]\nroot@openhands-workspace:/workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2 # \n[Command finished with exit code 1]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The response structure indicates that the `send_email` method is returning a dictionary with `ResponseMetadata`, but it does not include a `MessageId`. This suggests that the mocking might not be correctly applied to return the expected structure.\n\nLet's adjust the script to ensure the mocked method returns a dictionary with a `MessageId` key. I'll modify the script to achieve this.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/getmoto__moto__4.2/reproduce_error.py\", \"old_text\": \"\\n        assert \\\"mocked-message-id\\\" in response, \\\"