n- [x] New feature\r\n- [ ] Documentation / docstrings\r\n- [ ] Tests\r\n- [ ] Other\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I've run the latest [black](https://github.com/psf/black) with default args on new code.\r\n- [x] I've updated CHANGELOG.md and CONTRIBUTORS.md where appropriate.\r\n- [x] I've added tests for new code.\r\n- [x] I accept that @willmcgugan may be pedantic in the code review.\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nOptional flag for `Prompt.ask` allowing case-insensitive responses. Just add `case_sensitive=False` to the command options:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom rich.prompt import Prompt\r\nname = Prompt.ask(\"Enter your name\", choices=[\"Paul\", \"Jessica\", \"Duncan\"], default=\"Paul\", case_sensitive=False)\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow, it would accept \"paul\" or \"Paul\" as valid responses. Defaults to True, which is the usual result.\r\n\r\n\r\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll localize with the graph tools first, starting from the symbols named in the issue.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"search_similar_code\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"PromptBase\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "rich_3052", "repo": "Textualize/rich", "base_commit": "7a168a27c5097805b3bafa495f35e3955004ff4a", "files": ["rich/prompt.py"], "symbols": ["PromptBase", "__init__", "ask", "check_choice"], "n_hunks": 12, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_prompt.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live tool outputs. Read-file observations are snapshot.", "turns": 22, "generator": "gen_programmatic.py v1", "traj_turn": 0, "tool": "search_similar_code", "est_tokens": 1205, "split_from": "rich_3052"}}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an autonomous Python coding agent. You fix bugs and implement features in a Python repository by calling tools. Think briefly, then call exactly one tool per turn.\n\nYour tools:\n- run_command: run a shell command (pytest, python, grep, ls, git status). Keep output small. Never edit files with shell redirection or sed; use edit_file/write_file.\n- read_file: read a file (path, optional start_line/end_line, max 150 lines).\n- edit_file: make a small, precise edit (path, old_text, new_text). Match old_text exactly.\n- write_file: create a new file (path, content).\n- get_code_neighbors: list callers/callees of a symbol.\n- search_similar_code: find code similar to a symbol name.\n- get_code_subgraph: get the call-graph neighbourhood of a symbol.\n- get_status: check remaining time and tool-call budget.\n- submit_patch: finish and submit your patch. Call this only when the fix is verified by tests.\n\nWorkflow: reproduce the issue first (write a small script under /tmp and run it), localize with the graph tools and grep before reading files, make small incremental edits, re-run the relevant tests, then submit_patch. Never edit tests or test configuration (tests/, conftest.py, pytest.ini, pyproject.toml). Never leave scratch files inside the repo; use /tmp."}, {"role": "user", "content": "<uploaded_files>\n/workspace/python__mypy__0.970\n</uploaded_files>\nI've uploaded a python code repository in the directory python__mypy__0.970. Consider the following PR description:\n\n<pr_description>\nCrash when analysing qiskit\n**Crash Report**\r\n\r\nRunning mypy on a library where typing has recently been added causes a crash while analyzing this line:\r\nhttps://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-terra/blob/main/qiskit/circuit/library/blueprintcircuit.py#L72\r\n\r\n\r\n**Traceback**\r\n\r\n```\r\n/q/qiskit-terra/qiskit/circuit/library/blueprintcircuit.py:72: error: INTERNAL ERROR -- Please try using mypy master on Github:\r\nhttps:/