ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\ud83d\udc1b Fix OAuth2 scopes in OpenAPI in extra corner cases, parent dependency with scopes, sub-dependency security scheme without scopes\n\n\ud83d\udc1b Fix OAuth2 scopes in OpenAPI in extra corner cases, parent dependency with scopes, sub-dependency security scheme without scopes, and the same security scheme used as another sub-dependency without scopes in a different path operation.\r\n\r\nThe dependency without scopes would be cached for OpenAPI and for the one with scopes, it would render without scopes.\r\n\r\nThis also refactors the internals of how dependencies are handled, and how scopes and security schemes are passed through the code, removing duplication and simplifying parts, making them more robust and less error-prone. :muscle: \r\n\r\nThis should fix https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/14454 (strike 2 :baseball:)"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Re-running the repro after the edit to check the fix.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_14459.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "PASS: repro script now succeeds (no failure output after the fix)."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Repro passes. Now the narrowest relevant tests.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python -m pytest tests/test_security_oauth2_authorization_code_bearer_scopes_openapi.py tests/test_security_oauth2_authorization_code_bearer_scopes_openapi_simple.py -q\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "PASS: pytest tests/test_security_oauth2_authorization_code_bearer_scopes_openapi.py tests/test_security_oauth2_authorization_code_bearer_scopes_openapi_simple.py \u2014 all collected tests passed after the fix."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Tests pass. Confirming the diff touches only library code before submitting.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_status\", \"arguments\": {}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "git status --short:\n modified: fastapi/dependencies/models.py\n modified: fastapi/dependenc