\n\n## Pull Request\r\n\r\n\ud83d\udc1b Fix bug, allow empty path in path operation in prefixless router\r\n\r\nRelated to https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/15762\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease start with a GitHub Discussion.\r\n\r\nOnce a team member asks you to open a PR, create it and link the discussion here.\r\n\r\nObvious typo fixes can be made in a PR without starting a discussion.\r\n-->\r\n\r\nDiscussion: <!-- Link to the GitHub Discussion -->\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\n<!-- Write the description of your PR here -->\r\n\r\n## AI Disclaimer\r\n\r\n<!-- If using AI, write here the prompt and model used -->\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>AI transcript</summary>\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste here the entire AI transcript -->\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] This PR is an obvious typo fix, or it links to a GitHub Discussion for the proposed code change.\r\n- [ ] I added tests for the change.\r\n- [ ] The new or updated tests fail on the main branch and pass on this PR.\r\n- [ ] Coverage stays at 100%.\r\n- [ ] The documentation explains the change if needed.\r\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Before editing anything, I'll write a small repro script under /tmp that triggers the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/repro_fastapi_15763.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Repro for fastapi_15763 (programmatic replay; generic script).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/workspace\\\")\\n\\nfrom fastapi.routing import read_users  # noqa: F401\\n\\n# Reported failure (from the issue):\\n# \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix bug, allow empty path in path operation in prefixless router ## Pull Request \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix bug, allow empty path in path operation in prefixless router Related to https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issu...\\n# A faithful repro needs the exact failing call from the issue, so\\n# this script confirms the module imports and the symbol exists;\\n# the failure itself is triggered from the issue's example.\\nprint(\\\"repro ready:\\\", read_users)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "File written."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Running the repro to confirm the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_15763.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "FAIL: \ud83d\udc1b Fix bug, allow empty path in path operation in prefixless router ## Pull Request \ud83d\udc1b Fix bug, allow empty path in path operation in prefixless router Related to https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issu..."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/routing.py (hunk at line 2435).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/routing.py\", \"old_text\": \"                \\\"A path prefix must not end with '/', as the routes will start with '/'\\\"\\n            )\\n        else:\\n            for r in _iter_included_route_candidates(router.routes):\\n                path = getattr(r, \\\"path\\\", None)\\n                name = getattr(r, \\\"name\\\", \\\"unknown\\\")\\n                if path is not None and not path:\\n                    raise FastAPIError(\\n                        f\\\"Prefix and path cannot be both empty (path operation: {name})\\\"\", \"new_text\": \"                \\\"A path prefix must not end with '/', as the routes will start with '/'\\\"\\n            )\\n        else:\\n            for route, route_context in _iter_routes_with_context(router.routes):\\n                if route_context is None:\\n                    path = getattr(route, \\\"path\\\", None)\\n                    name = getattr(route, \\\"name\\\", \\\"unknown\\\")\\n                elif route_context.starlette_route is not None:\\n                    path = getattr(route_context.starlette_route, \\\"path\\\", None)\\n                    name = getattr(route_context.starlette_route, \\\"name\\\", \\\"unknown\\\")\\n                else:\\n                    path = route_context.path\\n                    name = route_context.name\\n                if path is not None and not path:\\n                    raise FastAPIError(\\n                        f\\\"Prefix and path cannot be both empty (path operation: {name})\\\"\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_15763", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "9a9c4ad5d06f5fe8ee6775a5aeaa2f83c854f263", "files": ["fastapi/routing.py"], "symbols": ["read_users", "_iter_included_route_candidates", "_iter_routes_with_context"], "n_hunks": 1, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_router_include_context.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live tool outputs. Read-file observations are snapshot.", "turns": 11, "generator": "gen_programmatic.py v1", "traj_turn": 6, "tool": "edit_file", "est_tokens": 1928, "split_from": "fastapi_15763"}}
