ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\ud83d\udc1b Update `ValidationError` schema to include `input` and `ctx`\n\n## Summary\r\n\r\nRelated to #10787\r\n\r\nThe OpenAPI `ValidationError` schema was outdated and didn't reflect the actual error format returned by Pydantic V2.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\nUpdated `validation_error_definition` in `fastapi/openapi/utils.py` to include:\r\n- `input`: The actual input value that caused the validation error  \r\n- `ctx`: Optional context dictionary with additional error information\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\nAll existing tests pass with the updated schema. The test snapshots have been updated to reflect the new schema structure."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Getting the surrounding call graph so I read only the files that matter.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_subgraph\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"utils\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"nodes\": [],\n \"edges\": [],\n \"files\": [\n  \"fastapi/openapi/utils.py\"\n ]\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Reading fastapi/openapi/utils.py around the suspect symbol.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"read_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/openapi/utils.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "fastapi/openapi/utils.py (lines 44-193 of 567):\n44|     \"properties\": {\n45|         \"loc\": {\n46|             \"title\": \"Location\",\n47|             \"type\": \"array\",\n48|             \"items\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"integer\"}]},\n49|         },\n50|         \"msg\": {\"title\": \"Message\", \"type\": \"string\"},\n51|         \"type\": {\"title\": \"Error Type\", \"type\": \"string\"},\n52|     },\n53|     \"required\": [\"loc\", \"msg\", \"type\"],\n54| }\n55| \n56| validation_error_response_definition = {\n57|     \"title\": \"HTTPValidationError\",\n58|     \"type\": \"object\",\n59|     \"properties\": {\n60|         \"detail\": {\n61|             \"title\": \"Detail\",\n62|             \"type\": \"array\",\n63|             \"items\": {\"$ref\": REF_PREFIX + \"ValidationError\"},\n64|         }\n65|     },\n66| }\n67| \n68| status_code_ranges: dict[str, str] = {\n69|     \"1XX\": \"Information\",\n70|     \"2XX\": \"Success\",\n71|     \"3XX\": \"Redirection\",\n72|     \"4XX\": \"Client Error\",\n73|     \"5XX\": \"Server Error\",\n74|     \"DEFAULT\": \"Default Response\",\n75| }\n76| \n77| \n78| def get_openapi_security_definitions(\n79|     flat_dependant: Dependant,\n80| ) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], list[dict[str, Any]]]:\n81|     security_definitions = {}\n82|     # Use a dict to merge scopes for same security scheme\n83|     operation_security_dict: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n84|     for security_dependency in flat_dependant._security_dependencies:\n85|         security_definition = jsonable_encoder(\n86|             security_dependency._security_scheme.model,\n87|             by_alias=True,\n88|             exclude_none=True,\n89|         )\n90|         security_name = security_dependency._security_scheme.scheme_name\n91|         security_definitions[security_name] = security_definition\n92|         # Merge scopes for the same security scheme\n93|         if security_name not in operation_security_dict:\n94|             operation_security_dict[security_name] = []\n95|         for scope in security_dependency.oauth_scopes or []:\n96|             if scope not in operat\n[... observation truncated ...]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Before editing anything, I'll write a small repro script under /tmp that triggers the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/repro_fastapi_14791.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Repro for fastapi_14791 (programmatic replay; generic script).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/workspace\\\")\\n\\nfrom fastapi.openapi.utils import utils  # noqa: F401\\n\\n# Reported failure (from the issue):\\n# \\ud83d\\udc1b Update `ValidationError` schema to include `input` and `ctx` ## Summary Related to #10787 The OpenAPI `ValidationError` schema was outdated and didn't reflect the actual error format returned by Pyd...\\n# A faithful repro needs the exact failing call from the issue, so\\n# this script confirms the module imports and the symbol exists;\\n# the failure itself is triggered from the issue's example.\\nprint(\\\"repro ready:\\\", utils)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "File written."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Running the repro to confirm the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_14791.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_14791", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "08924400c2c75533685148b029defcf6913f1def", "files": ["fastapi/openapi/utils.py"], "symbols": [], "n_hunks": 1, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_additional_properties.py", "tests/test_additional_properties_bool.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live tool outputs. Read-file observations are snapshot.", "turns": 11, "generator": "gen_programmatic.py v1", "traj_turn": 5, "tool": "run_command", "est_tokens": 1967, "split_from": "fastapi_14791"}}
