dding a user to the same group twice causes the group to become \"sticky.\"\n\nTo fix this, we need to modify the `add_user_to_group` method to check if the user is already in the group before adding them. Let's make this change.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/getmoto__moto__4.1/moto/iam/models.py\", \"old_text\": \"        group.users.append(user)\", \"new_text\": \"\\n        if user not in group.users:\\n            group.users.append(user)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "swegym-sft", "instance_id": "getmoto__moto__4.1", "traj_turn": 6, "tool": "edit_file", "est_tokens": 1985}}
