nStarlette 0.48.0 introduced `HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_CONTENT` as a new name for `HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY` and deprecated the old name due to RFC 9110; see https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/2939.\r\n\r\nI updated all instances ~to the new name and increased the lower bound on the Starlette version~ to use the literal integer or string value `422`/`\"422\"` instead of either `HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_CONTENT` or `HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY`, which makes FastAPI compatible with Starlette >=0.48 without deprecation warnings while preserving backwards compatibility with Starlette<0.48.\r\n\r\n@Kludex, FYI."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll localize with the graph tools first, starting from the symbols named in the issue.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"search_similar_code\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"validation_exception_handler\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"symbol\": \"validation_exception_handler\",\n \"matches\": [\n  {\n   \"file\": \"docs_src/handling_errors/tutorial005.py\",\n   \"line\": 11,\n   \"kind\": \"definition\"\n  }\n ]\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "validation_exception_handler is defined in docs_src/handling_errors/tutorial005.py. Checking its callers and callees before reading any file.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_neighbors\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"validation_exception_handler\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_14077", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "16d75d90eb96976a57b94cc24e4018859cd54c4d", "files": ["docs_src/handling_errors/tutorial005.py", "fastapi/exception_handlers.py", "fastapi/openapi/utils.py"], "symbols": ["validation_exception_handler", "http_exception_handler", "request_validation_exception_handler", "get_openapi_path"], "n_hunks": 6, "n_files": 3, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_enforce_once_required_parameter.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live tool outputs. Read-file observations are snapshot.", "turns": 18, "generator": "gen_programmatic.py v1", "traj_turn": 1, "tool": "get_code_neighbors", "est_tokens": 1269, "split_from": "fastapi_14077"}}
